{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC — hand-built from the documented response shapes in Yahoo's official",
    "Fantasy Sports API guide and from published wrapper-library samples (yfpy,",
    "yahoo_fantasy_api). NOT a live capture. Yahoo API access is gated behind an",
    "approval application and NO live call has ever been made from this repo.",
    "Replace with a real redacted capture once API access is approved.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED 2026-08-11 (not captured on any date).",
    "MODELS: GET /fantasy/v2/league/449.l.529351/teams/roster;week=5/players/",
    "            stats;type=week;week=5?format=json",
    "",
    "REDACTION: all identifiers invented — team keys, team names and manager",
    "GUIDs (FAKEGUID...) are fake. Player names are real NFL players with",
    "PLAUSIBLE BUT UNVERIFIED numeric ids.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS COMMITTED: this is the CHAINED form, and it is the answer to",
    "yahoo_roster_week.json's first claim. A plain roster response ends each",
    "player at selected_position and carries no points at all; only this deeper",
    "path returns player_stats and player_points, and it is a SECOND request for",
    "every league-week (Yahoo's ;out= is one level deep and cannot take",
    "parameters, so there is no way to fold it into the roster call). Fifteen",
    "seasons times seventeen weeks is a real request budget, and it is the only",
    "route to HISTORICAL BENCH POINTS — the numbers needed to ask 'what did this",
    "manager leave on the bench?', which no Yahoo UI will ever show you again.",
    "",
    "⚠️ points only exist in a LEAGUE context. Fetching a player resource bare",
    "returns raw stats and NO points, because points are the league's stat",
    "modifiers applied to those stats. That is why every stats request in the",
    "adapter is made under a /league/ path.",
    "",
    "SHAPE HAZARDS DELIBERATELY PRESENT:",
    "  1. ⚠️ THE NUMERIC SUB-RESOURCE WRAPPER, same as yahoo_roster_week.json:",
    "     'roster' is an object whose players collection hangs off the key \"0\"",
    "     (yfpy's own data key list is [\"team\",\"roster\",\"0\",\"players\"]). See the",
    "     KNOWN DISAGREEMENT note at the end.",
    "  2. The player resource now has FOUR members: [ [metadata...],",
    "     {selected_position}, {player_stats}, {player_points} ]. The sub-resource",
    "     indices SHIFT relative to the un-chained roster response — same league,",
    "     same week, different member count. Hardcoding an index against one",
    "     response shape breaks against the other; nothing here may be read",
    "     positionally.",
    "  3. STAT VALUE \"-\" IS NOT ZERO. Yahoo returns the literal string '-' for a",
    "     stat the player has no value for (Josh Allen's receiving yards, stat 12,",
    "     below). to_float('-') is None, and None is correct: he did not record",
    "     zero receiving yards, the stat does not apply. Stat 6 (interceptions) on",
    "     the same player IS a literal \"0\" — he genuinely threw none. Those two",
    "     must not collapse into one another.",
    "  4. player_points.total is a STRING with a decimal ('27.94'); one team's",
    "     kicker returns the whole number '9' with no decimal point.",
    "  5. THE BENCH PLAYER HAS POINTS. Jerry Jeudy is in the BN slot and still",
    "     carries a full stat line and a points total. That is the entire value of",
    "     this endpoint and the assertion worth writing.",
    "  6. The stats array is a plain LIST of {\"stat\": {...}} — no numeric-key",
    "     wrapper at this level, unlike the collections above it. Yahoo mixes both",
    "     conventions inside a single response.",
    "",
    "TRUNCATED HARD: 2 teams of 12, 3 players each, and ~5 stats per player",
    "instead of the full ~30-line NFL stat block. Reason: the stat rows are a",
    "uniform loop, and what is being proven here is the SHAPE (stats + points",
    "present, '-' vs '0', bench included), not the breadth of the stat",
    "dictionary. Scoring breadth is covered by yahoo_league_settings_auction.json.",
    "",
    "⚠️ KNOWN DISAGREEMENT WITH THE SHIPPED PARSER, 2026-08-11. Against parse.py",
    "at PARSER_VERSION 1.0.0 this file parses to 0 stat rows and 0 point rows,",
    "SILENTLY — no exception — because flatten_resource() does not descend into",
    "the numeric-key members of an OBJECT resource, so get(roster, \"players\") is",
    "MISSING. Reported to the parser author rather than papered over; deleting the",
    "\"0\" wrapper would make the fixture green and the pipeline wrong against the",
    "real API.",
    "",
    "EXPECTED ONCE THE PARSER HANDLES THE WRAPPER (measured by hoisting roster",
    "[\"0\"] in a harness, with parse.py untouched):",
    "    fantasy_player_week_stats  25     fantasy_player_week_points  6",
    "    Josh Allen stat 6 (\"0\")  -> 0.0        stat 12 (\"-\")  -> None",
    "    bench player nfl.p.32700 -> points_provider 23.2",
    "Those are the numbers to assert."
  ],
